# AI Agents Guide — __PLUGIN_NAME__

Welcome, AI Agent! This WordPress block plugin is built by Block Rig: **Bun is
the only runtime** (bundler, transpiler, watcher). No esbuild, no webpack, no
SCSS, no PostCSS.

## 1. Source files only

- NEVER edit anything under `blocks/*/build/` — it is generated.
- Editor code: `blocks/<name>/src/*.tsx`. Frontend render: `blocks/<name>/render.php`.
- Block config: `blocks/<name>/block.json` (apiVersion 3).

## 2. Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `bun run build` | Build all blocks (JS via Bun.build, CSS via Lightning CSS) |
| `NODE_ENV=production bun run build` | Production (minified, no maps) |
| `bun run dev` | Dev server: reverse-proxies the WP site + live-reload + per-block rebuild |
| `bun run dev --proxy http://my-site.local` | Same, target via flag (alternative to config) |
| `bun run block:new <slug> --type static\|dynamic\|php` | Scaffold a new block |
| `bun run lint` | TypeScript check + stylelint CSS budget |
| `bun test` | Unit tests (config, wp-externals, CSS compile, lint budget) |
| `bun run check` | Full pre-flight: lint + test |
| `bun run zip` | Production build + package as WP-installable `<slug>.zip` |

## 3. Configuration first

`blockrig.config.json` is the single source of truth: plugin slug, block
namespace, block directory, CSS targets, dev-server target. Never hardcode
these in scripts — read them via `scripts/lib/config.ts`. Set
`devServer.proxyTarget` to the local WP site URL for `bun run dev`.

## 4. CSS conventions (plain modern CSS — no SCSS, ever)

The `.stylelintrc` budget is **enforced** — `bun run lint` fails on violations:

- **Specificity budget (0,4,1)** — no IDs; keep selectors shallow; prefer
  `:where()` to lower weight.
- **Nesting depth ≤ 3.**
- **No `!important`.**
- **Sass-style `&` concatenation is banned** — native CSS nesting does not
  concatenate; `&__x` compiles to a broken selector. Write full class names.
- `@custom-media` is supported (compiled via Lightning CSS `drafts.customMedia`
  — already enabled in `scripts/build.ts`; don't remove it).
- Logical properties, `:has()`, container queries: all fine.

## 5. Block types

| Type | Files | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `dynamic` | block.json, src/index.tsx, src/edit.tsx, render.php, src/style.css | PHP renders; save returns null |
| `static` | block.json, src/index.tsx, src/edit.tsx, src/save.tsx, src/style.css | Markup saved in post content |
| `php` | block.json (`supports.autoRegister`), render.php, src/style.css | No JS build at all |

Optional entries per block: `src/view.ts` → `build/view.js` (frontend JS — add
`"viewScript": "file:./build/view.js"` to block.json) and
`src/editorStyle.css` → `build/editorStyle.css` (editor-only styles — add the
`editorStyle` handle). Add handles only when the files exist — WordPress
warns on missing assets.

## 6. wp.* globals

Editor code imports `@wordpress/*` / `react` normally — the build remaps them
to the `window.wp.*` globals WordPress enqueues (see
`scripts/lib/wp-externals.ts`). Nothing WP-provided is ever bundled.